            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="0868" n="860" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg860"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/1058: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-07T15:00:00+00:00">December 7, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 7—11:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1403. From Rublee. We have been informed that the Brussels meeting with Pell and
                    Cotton tomorrow has been canceled. Preliminary information received through our
                    German intermediary here is that there were too many cooks; that the French had
                    taken up the general problem and specific financial points with Ribbentrop; and
                    that the latter had been obliged to take a position. [Rublee.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
